# TestInbox SMTP edge — transport map. RENDERED by deploy/mail-edge/render.sh.
#
# Anything not matched here falls through to `default_transport = discard`
# (main.cf), so an empty map means the edge accepts nothing onward and emits
# nothing. That is the intended DORMANT state of the real host.
#
# The postmaster line routes postmaster@ to a LOCAL Maildir. The lookup happens
# at DELIVERY time, after the message is accepted and queued, so the SMTP
# conversation is byte-identical to any other recipient.
__EDGE_POSTMASTER_LINE__
# The relay line points at TestInbox ingestion. The real host writes it only
# when EDGE_RELAY_TARGET is set, and today leaves it absent — which renders
# `<domain> discard:` and is why the dormant host cannot prove ADR-025.
# The rehearsal MUST render the production relay form, or an unknown-recipient
# test proves nothing: the edge would discard the message itself instead of
# relaying it for ingestion to discard. Brackets suppress MX lookup.
__EDGE_RELAY_LINE__
